 dict(pmid='', doi='10.1016/j.apr.2026.103282', journal='Atmospheric Pollution Research', title='Associations of Visual Landscape Quantity versus Configuration with Air Pollution along Urban Streets: A Case Study of Xuzhou, China', short='Atmos Pollut Res Xuzhou street view visual landscape quantity configuration air pollution', design='Metadata only: no abstract in Crossref at issue time', pm='Not stated (street-level air pollution, metric not given in metadata)', geo='China (Xuzhou)', endpoint='Not stated', tier='C', basis='Not stated', affil='', n='Metadata only. An Atmospheric Pollution Research case study of Xuzhou relating the quantity versus the spatial configuration of the visual street landscape to air pollution along urban streets. Crossref carried no abstract, so the pollutant, measurement method (fixed, mobile or sensor-based) and any effect size are unknown and no finding is asserted. Relevance: possibly direct - street-view landscape features are increasingly used as predictors in hyperlocal exposure models fed by mobile or low-cost sensor data; whether this study measured PM, and how, needs the full text.', sub=corpus.EXPO),
